{"name":"Sea Sparkle","hex":"#469ba7","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"sea sparkle","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The bioluminescent dinoflagellate Noctiluca scintillans (syn. Noctiluca miliaris), that causes some seafire.","The glow created by these dinoflagellates; seafire."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sea_sparkle"}],"entries":[{"title":"Milky seas effect","blocks":[{"text":"Milky seas, sometimes confused with mareel, are a luminous phenomenon in the ocean in which large areas of seawater appear to glow diffusely and continuously. Such occurrences glow brightly enough at night to be visible from satellites orbiting Earth. Unlike flashing waves or red-tide luminescence caused by algae such as dinoflagellates, milky seas originate from luminous bacteria."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/19/Milky_sea_nightcolor5x5.jpg/330px-Milky_sea_nightcolor5x5.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Milky_seas_effect","wikidata":"Q1916842"},{"title":"Sea","blocks":[{"text":"A sea is a very large body of salty water. The term has two distinct meanings. The first is the interconnected body of seawater that spans most of Earth, known as the sea or the ocean. The second is a named body of water: usually either a marginal sea, or a large, nearly landlocked body of water."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg/330px-Mediterranean_Sea_16.61811E_38.99124N.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sea","wikidata":"Q165"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png/500px-Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7b/Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png/500px-Mixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AMixed_phytoplankton_community_2.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flask_of_luminous_bacteria.jpg/500px-Flask_of_luminous_bacteria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flask_of_luminous_bacteria.jpg/1280px-Flask_of_luminous_bacteria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/18/Flask_of_luminous_bacteria.jpg/500px-Flask_of_luminous_bacteria.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A culture of luminous bacteria, showing the diffuse uniform light that characterizes milky seas.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFlask_of_luminous_bacteria.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/500px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/1280px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1c/BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg/500px-BlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Composite images of the Earth created by NASA in 2001","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABlueMarble-2001-2002.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2d/Propagation_du_tsunami_en_profondeur_variable.gif/330px-Propagation_du_tsunami_en_profondeur_variable.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_conte